    "lightning_ready": true,
    "bitcoin_integration": "El Salvador was the first country to make Bitcoin legal tender (Sept 7, 2021). Under a $1.4bn / 40-month IMF program (Dec 2024), Legislative Decree No. 199 was gazetted Jan 30 2025 and took effect ~May 1 2025, dismantling the compulsory framework: merchant acceptance of Bitcoin is now voluntary (not mandatory), the government's Chivo wallet participation is being phased out (by end-July 2025 per IMF terms), and the state does not voluntarily accumulate more Bitcoin. As of 2026 Bitcoin is effectively voluntary tender — most analysts treat the compulsory 'legal tender' obligation as rescinded while the USD remains the dominant currency for wages, prices and taxes; the state retains its existing Bitcoin holdings. The country remains strongly crypto-promotional at the government level despite the legal rollback."
